            {
                "entry_id": "094eb69e-705c-3286-bd81-f7e3740f60d4",
                "word": "knocker",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "3d7fd0b4-1318-48d0-b5d6-f3ab80a5a337",
                        "entry_id": "094eb69e-705c-3286-bd81-f7e3740f60d4",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "knockers"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "ce245200-5ce0-3a47-b57d-e59610a23611",
                        "entry_id": "094eb69e-705c-3286-bd81-f7e3740f60d4",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A device, usually hinged with a striking plate, used for knocking on a door."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "a9f46ea8-cee0-4824-a003-e8596b495140",
                                "sense_id": "ce245200-5ce0-3a47-b57d-e59610a23611",
                                "text": "Knockers in this part of the world seem intended for ornament only, — nobody seems to pay any attention to them when they’re used."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "bc9ee481-0e71-4756-8f8c-928e8b601791",
                                "sense_id": "ce245200-5ce0-3a47-b57d-e59610a23611",
                                "text": "His tongue became a staircase, his uvula the knocker / Of an ornate wooden door that led me straight into my future"
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "79b9eee2-c152-3b73-b965-6bcfc34f36c7",
                        "entry_id": "094eb69e-705c-3286-bd81-f7e3740f60d4",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A person who knocks."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "fac31a00-6f3e-4e4e-8076-4209060183e6",
                                "sense_id": "79b9eee2-c152-3b73-b965-6bcfc34f36c7",
                                "text": "He was a loud knocker. Despite my usual timidity, after a bit I opened the door."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "80377429-27a9-3c4c-a96c-35f869dceab7",
                        "entry_id": "094eb69e-705c-3286-bd81-f7e3740f60d4",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A critic; one who disparages."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "fc8f2082-281f-4668-9362-c923d3ee838d",
                                "sense_id": "80377429-27a9-3c4c-a96c-35f869dceab7",
                                "text": "\"I try to give everybody credit,\" declared the old man. \"I am not a knocker. I am not too good for this world.\""
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "72b76ea8-c44a-317b-8625-9833ab5b4100",
                        "entry_id": "094eb69e-705c-3286-bd81-f7e3740f60d4",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A person who knocks (denigrates) something."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "derogatory",
                            "informal"
                        ],
                        "examples": []
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "42814621-79b8-3dfe-9eb8-22c677db41f7",
                        "entry_id": "094eb69e-705c-3286-bd81-f7e3740f60d4",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A person's breast, especially if large."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "plural-normally",
                            "slang"
                        ],
                        "examples": []
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "32e32694-33a2-355c-b562-c3063c0f5fd9",
                        "entry_id": "094eb69e-705c-3286-bd81-f7e3740f60d4",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A dwarf, goblin, or sprite imagined to dwell in mines and to indicate the presence of ore by knocking."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "archaic"
                        ],
                        "examples": []
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "e551f9d0-c348-30a2-9b57-6de537cda33f",
                        "entry_id": "094eb69e-705c-3286-bd81-f7e3740f60d4",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A mechanical device in a pinball table that produces a loud percussive noise."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "4e64453e-890b-4e46-9fc3-b541bcd14725",
                                "sense_id": "e551f9d0-c348-30a2-9b57-6de537cda33f",
                                "text": "A good game needs color, lights, bells, gongs, and knockers, all to assure the player he is making progress[…]"
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "c954d5fe-3c8f-349d-b2a5-5e4db920620d",
                        "entry_id": "094eb69e-705c-3286-bd81-f7e3740f60d4",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A person who is strikingly handsome or otherwise admirable; a stunner."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "dated",
                            "slang"
                        ],
                        "examples": []
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "fb4142e6-2555-3e7f-aa13-c4f9b47f7985",
                        "entry_id": "094eb69e-705c-3286-bd81-f7e3740f60d4",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A large cockroach, especially Blaberus giganteus, of semitropical America, which is able to produce a loud knocking sound."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": []
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "b0b295ea-128c-32c8-9bda-05f87bb8a49c",
                        "entry_id": "094eb69e-705c-3286-bd81-f7e3740f60d4",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A large, boulder-shaped outcrop of bedrock in an otherwise low-lying landscape, chiefly associated with a mélange."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": []
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "cf393d4b-ba92-342f-a71e-3010782973d3",
                        "entry_id": "094eb69e-705c-3286-bd81-f7e3740f60d4",
                        "glosses": [
                            "One who defaults on payment of a wager."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "slang"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "74c5a5aa-3d53-4722-a454-459d6f6f2d74",
                                "sense_id": "cf393d4b-ba92-342f-a71e-3010782973d3",
                                "text": "To the consternation of those who believed that bookies were 'knockers' (defaulters), he paid his losses with alacrity […]"
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "ac290e88-16b4-3684-aab1-9ab6699dd142",
                        "entry_id": "094eb69e-705c-3286-bd81-f7e3740f60d4",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A gun."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "slang"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "7a69aa3a-4302-4dfe-be55-df091e822cab",
                                "sense_id": "ac290e88-16b4-3684-aab1-9ab6699dd142",
                                "text": "Lay down on that 'Tussin, I think I'ma snooze (Like, like what?)\nWe keep knockers like this shit essential\n.22 long rifles, these bullets like pencils\nHomicide, bodies drop when we bend through"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "1243acbd-11ef-4b00-a9af-0d78f226f317",
                                "sense_id": "ac290e88-16b4-3684-aab1-9ab6699dd142",
                                "text": "Last opper we caught had to pop 'em, shouldn't've left out his crib without knockers"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "832213ce-81e4-4e64-a368-4fb8b3f52d70",
                                "sense_id": "ac290e88-16b4-3684-aab1-9ab6699dd142",
                                "text": "Dotty my holster, totin on this knocker (Grrah, grrah)\nIf we see the'Ds, bitch, move proper"
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "27c76126-6d92-3188-844a-30d56c26b953",
                        "entry_id": "094eb69e-705c-3286-bd81-f7e3740f60d4",
                        "glosses": [
                            "An undercover policeman."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "slang"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "02d2e2f0-4c76-436d-b8e2-aa1bdf4fef25",
                                "sense_id": "27c76126-6d92-3188-844a-30d56c26b953",
                                "text": "The knockers around better do what I say so"
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "56396759-1544-4951-9946-9f1daa6502c7",
